\begin{flushleft}
\footnotesize{This figure shows that the smoothed inflation estimates (red) produced by our nonlinear filter closely track U.S. inflation data (blue), despite relying solely on SPF data. For comparison, we also plot the one-quarter-ahead SPF forecasts made in the same quarter (SPF1Q, black). The model’s fitting error (dashed red) and the SPF1Q error (dashed black) are shown as the respective gaps from observed inflation. }
